From cb42d5123dca8b0c48d53e928e56aa4f774bce28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:31:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 110/120] gui: check that every UI language carries every key

The GUI has no fallback to English, so a key missing from a language
shows up as its raw name. scripts/check-translations.mjs (npm test, no
dependencies) compares each language with en: missing or extra keys,
empty values, placeholder mismatches, keys defined twice in a block,
and languages missing from LanguageSwitcher. A light Translations
workflow runs it on pushes and on pull requests, forks included, ahead
of the pt-BR contribution offered in issue #14.

What it found on the way:
- editServer was defined twice in every language; the later "Edit
  server" silently won, so the server list's button also read "Edit
  server". The dead first entry is removed, which keeps today's text.
- t() returned the key for an empty string, so the About tab showed
  the raw "basedOn". An empty string is now returned as is.
